# This becomes a portfolio project

This is something I'd expect from a **Senior/Staff AI Platform Engineer**:

* Practical.
* Extensible.
* Demonstrates deep understanding of transformer internals.
* Useful to other engineers.

## How we'll build it

We'll do this in **12 milestones**, each ending with a working, testable feature.

| Milestone | Deliverable                                    |
| --------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| 1         | Project scaffold + CLI + config loader         |
| 2         | Architecture inspector                         |
| 3         | Attention inspector (MHA/GQA/MQA + KV cache)   |
| 4         | FFN inspector                                  |
| 5         | MoE inspector                                  |
| 6         | Memory estimator                               |
| 7         | GPU estimator                                  |
| 8         | Module introspection (load model when desired) |
| 9         | Model comparison                               |
| 10        | Exporters (JSON/Markdown/CSV/HTML)             |
| 11        | Unit tests + CI                                |
| 12        | PyPI packaging + documentation                 |

I recommend this approach because every milestone produces a usable tool, and by the end you'll have a polished project that showcases both AI architecture knowledge and software engineering skills. We'll start with Milestone 1 in the next step.
